From 8bba9599a5d498e197ed7458c24eb54a3ef92e7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 12:02:10 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(pr-monitor): address CodeRabbit review threads on PR #367
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- journal: scope dedup to snapshot appliedSeq cursor, not whole history —
  a fail→green→fail cycle on the same sha re-emits instead of being
  suppressed forever (CR journal.js:83). Regression test added.
- journal+monitor: serialize the read→diff→dedup→append→snapshot critical
  section across processes with a crash-recoverable lock-directory
  (withJournalLock) so concurrent passes never interleave appends or reuse
  a seq (CR monitor.js:78). Concurrent-append test added.
- shepherd: wire the DEFAULT failed-check enrichment into `events` so a
  plain `forge shepherd events` attaches check.failed log excerpts, and
  forward an injected enrich to pollEvents (CR shepherd.js:157). Integration
  test added.
- pr-pull: fail closed when the base refresh fails — fetchBase failure now
  records `unreadable` (not just degraded) so a stale ref can't yield a
  false-clean verdict; verdict → UNKNOWN (CR pr-pull.js:1073). Test added.
- docs: rename design.md → plan.md per the work-artifact convention and
  update the gather.js reference (CR design.md:1).
- test/commands/shepherd.test.js:133 duplication already absent in HEAD.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
